From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:52:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/23] perf(scheduler): run EE threads on fibers instead of
 unwinding to switch

Ported from Sinan Karakaya's PS2Recomp fork (GPL-3.0), commits 8b83b2b,
684c3ce, e44c029, 3a2bb26, b26188d and a12955b: EeFiber (native x86-64
and ARM64 switches, Win32 fibers, ucontext fallback) and its tests are
taken as they are; the scheduler side is rewritten against this tree.

Each guest thread runs on its own stack. A yield (transferIfRequested)
and sleep, semaphore and event-flag waits suspend that stack instead of
throwing EeDispatcherTransfer through the guest's whole C++ call chain.
On macOS every such throw walked the unwind tables of the recompiled
binary frame by frame; SLES-55605's movie player yields thousands of
times a frame and ran at 2-3 fps. Waits with a completion, thread exit
and the executor's own stack still throw. A self-deleted thread's
record lives until its fiber has stopped, and a thread made dormant
while suspended drops its stale fiber.

Co-Authored-By: Sinan Karakaya <karakaya.sinan@proton.me>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
